Payload:
Found 7 concrete issues:

1. `instruction_file_disobeyed` — severity 3, confidence 0.99  
   Location: `convex/integrations.ts:195`  
   The new integration queries use unbounded `.collect()` calls, contrary to `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md`, which requires bounded `.take()` or pagination. Folios with extensive feedback or suggestions can exceed Convex read limits and make the bearer API fail.
   ```ts
       if (wanted.has("feedback")) {
         const [notes, replies] = await Promise.all([
           ctx.db
             .query("personaNotes")
             .withIndex("by_userId_folioId", (q) =>
               q.eq("userId", userId).eq("folioId", folioId),
             )
             .collect(),
           ctx.db
             .query("personaReplies")
             .withIndex("by_userId_folioId", (q) =>
               q.eq("userId", userId).eq("folioId", folioId),
             )
             .collect(),
         ]);
   ```
   The same violation recurs in `getFeedback` and suggestion retrieval.

2. `test_coverage` — severity 4, confidence 1.0  
   Location: `convex/integrations.test.ts:8`  
   All newly added backend integration tests are skipped by the repository’s actual `bun test` command because `import.meta.glob` is unavailable there. Dagger also invokes only `bun test`, not Vitest. Token ownership, digest-only storage, conflict detection, citation behavior, and search therefore have no enforced test coverage.
   ```ts
   const supportsViteModules = typeof import.meta.glob === "function";
   const modules = supportsViteModules ? import.meta.glob("./**/*.ts") : {};
   const describeConvex = supportsViteModules ? describe : describe.skip;
   ```
   Direct verification produced three skipped tests and zero executed tests.

3. `insecure_code` — severity 4, confidence 0.98  
   Location: `packages/twyne-tools/src/config.ts:35`  
   Arbitrary remote HTTP endpoints are accepted even though every request transmits the personal bearer token and potentially manuscript contents. HTTP should only be allowed for explicitly recognized loopback development endpoints.
   ```ts
     if (url.protocol !== "https:" && url.protocol !== "http:") {
       throw new Error("Twyne API URL must use http or https");
     }
     return url.toString().replace(/\/$/, "");
   ```

4. `insecure_code` — severity 4, confidence 0.96  
   Location: `src/utils/standard-site-reader.server.ts:71`  
   The SSRF check blocks literal private IPs and selected hostnames but accepts public hostnames resolving to private addresses or DNS-rebinding targets. An attacker controlling a valid PLC DID document can cause Twyne’s server-side reader to fetch a fixed XRPC path from an internal HTTPS service. DNS resolution and IP-range validation must occur before connecting and remain pinned through the request.
   ```ts
   function safeServiceEndpoint(value: unknown): string | null {
     if (typeof value !== "string") return null;
     try {
       const url = new URL(value);
       const host = url.hostname.toLowerCase();
       if (url.protocol !== "https:" || url.username || url.password) return null;
       if (
         host === "localhost" ||
         host.endsWith(".localhost") ||
         host.endsWith(".local") ||
         host.endsWith(".internal") ||
         /^\d{1,3}(?:\.\d{1,3}){3}$/.test(host) ||
         host.startsWith("[")
       ) {
         return null;
       }
       return url.origin;
     } catch {
       return null;
     }
   }
   ```

5. `fails_silently` — severity 4, confidence 0.96  
   Location: `src/utils/standard-site.ts:135`  
   Every `getRecord` failure is treated as a stale cache. A timeout, authorization failure, or PDS 5xx is silently converted into `current = null`, after which `putRecord` can overwrite an existing publication with a minimal reconstructed record and discard its description or other fields. Only a confirmed record-not-found response should enter the recreation path; other failures should be surfaced.
   ```ts
     let current: UnknownRecord | null = null;
     try {
       const existing = await agent.com.atproto.repo.getRecord({
         repo: parsed.did,
         collection: STANDARD_SITE_PUBLICATION_COLLECTION,
         rkey: parsed.rkey,
       });
       current = existing.data.value as UnknownRecord;
     } catch {
       // A stale local cache is allowed to recreate its deterministic record.
     }

     const url = standardSitePublicationUrl(parsed.did, parsed.rkey);
     await agent.com.atproto.repo.putRecord({
       repo: parsed.did,
       collection: STANDARD_SITE_PUBLICATION_COLLECTION,
       rkey: parsed.rkey,
       record: publicationRecord(current, { name, url }),
     });
   ```

6. `error_handling_missing` — severity 3, confidence 0.97  
   Location: `packages/twyne-tools/src/client.ts:68`  
   API requests have no default timeout, and all CLI/MCP call sites omit a signal. A stalled connection can therefore hang an interactive CLI command or MCP tool indefinitely. The client should create a default timeout signal and compose it with a caller-provided signal.
   ```ts
     async request<T>(request: IntegrationRequest, signal?: AbortSignal): Promise<T> {
       let response: Response;
       try {
         response = await this.fetchImpl(this.endpoint, {
           method: "POST",
           headers: {
             authorization: `Bearer ${this.accessToken}`,
             "content-type": "application/json",
             accept: "application/json",
             "user-agent": "@twyne/tools",
           },
           body: JSON.stringify(request),
           signal,
         });
   ```

7. `error_handling_missing` — severity 2, confidence 0.98  
   Location: `src/routes/settings/index.tsx:947`  
   Clipboard writes can reject because of permissions, insecure contexts, or unavailable clipboard APIs. This handler neither catches the rejection nor exposes a recoverable notice, leaving the token-copy action with an unhandled failure.
   ```ts
     const handleCopyIntegrationToken = $(async () => {
       if (!store.newIntegrationToken) return;
       await navigator.clipboard.writeText(store.newIntegrationToken);
       store.integrationTokenCopied = true;
     });
   ```

No material findings in `documentation_implementation_mismatch` or `user_request_artifacts_left_in_code`.

