Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER
Task name: /root
Sender: /root/correctness_audit
Payload:
Found 7 issues in the assigned categories.

1. `type_safety_violation` — severity 4, confidence 0.99  
Location: `convex/integrations.ts`  
The integration accepts arbitrary citation objects and validates only `title`, `id`, and `accessedAt`. A title-only citation is explicitly valid in the CLI/MCP contract, but existing `BibEntry` requires `url: string`, and citation UI render paths immediately call `entry.url.replace(...)`. Thus a documented valid API request can persist data that crashes the citations panel/apparatus when rendered. Other optional fields can likewise be non-strings through direct HTTP/CLI archive input.

```ts
  args: {
    userId: v.string(),
    folioId: v.string(),
    entries: v.array(v.any()),
  },
  returns: v.object({ saved: v.number() }),
  handler: async (ctx, { userId, folioId, entries }) => {
    if (entries.length > 100) {
      throw new Error("At most 100 citations may be saved at once");
    }
    const row = await ctx.db
      .query("bibliographies")
      .withIndex("by_userId", (q) => q.eq("userId", userId))
      .first();
    const merged = [...(row?.entries ?? [])];
    for (const raw of entries) {
      if (!raw || typeof raw !== "object" || Array.isArray(raw)) {
        throw new Error("Each citation must be an object");
      }
      const entry = { ...raw, folioId } as Record<string, unknown>;
      if (typeof entry.title !== "string" || !entry.title.trim()) {
        throw new Error("Each citation needs a title");
      }
      if (typeof entry.id !== "string" || !entry.id.trim()) {
        entry.id = crypto.randomUUID();
      }
      if (typeof entry.accessedAt !== "number") entry.accessedAt = Date.now();
```

2. `logic_error` — severity 3, confidence 0.98  
Location: `convex/integrations.ts`  
Token creation has no per-account cap, while the only management query returns the newest 50. Once a writer creates a 51st token, an older still-valid bearer credential disappears from Settings and its ID is unavailable for `revokeToken`; only deleting the account can revoke it. Enforce the same cap at creation or paginate/list every active token.

```ts
    const rows = await ctx.db
      .query("integrationTokens")
      .withIndex("by_userId", (q) => q.eq("userId", userId))
      .order("desc")
      .take(50);
```

3. `runtime_error_risk` — severity 3, confidence 0.96  
Location: `convex/integrations.ts`  
`searchFolios` performs one query and materializes the complete HTML document for every folio, up to the allowed 500. Accounts with sufficiently many or large manuscripts will exceed Convex transaction byte/read limits, so search returns a generic integration failure. The result `limit` only limits output after all reads and provides no protection.

```ts
    for (const folio of (foliosRow?.folios ?? []).slice(
      0,
      MAX_FOLIOS_PER_ACCOUNT,
    )) {
      const content = await ctx.db
        .query("folioContent")
        .withIndex("by_userId_folioId", (q) =>
          q.eq("userId", userId).eq("folioId", folio.id),
        )
        .first();
      const text = (content?.html ?? "")
        .replace(/<[^>]+>/g, " ")
        .replace(/\s+/g, " ")
        .trim();
```

4. `incorrect_algorithm` — severity 4, confidence 0.98  
Location: `src/utils/standard-site-reader.server.ts`  
Publication loading issues one `listRecords(limit=100)` request and ignores the cursor, so publication indexes silently omit every document after 100. More seriously, the well-known verification route calls this same full publication loader even though it only needs the publication record. Because `fetchJson` applies a roughly 1 MB cap to the combined list response, enough document content makes an otherwise valid publication’s verification endpoint and publication page return 404.

```ts
  const url = new URL("/xrpc/com.atproto.repo.listRecords", pds);
  url.searchParams.set("repo", did);
  url.searchParams.set("collection", STANDARD_SITE_DOCUMENT_COLLECTION);
  url.searchParams.set("limit", "100");
  url.searchParams.set("reverse", "true");
  const envelope = recordObject(await fetchJson(url, fetcher));
  const records = Array.isArray(envelope?.records) ? envelope.records : [];
```

5. `async_correctness` — severity 2, confidence 0.97  
Location: `src/routes/dossier/refine/index.tsx`  
Both refine completion handlers fire `dossier_completed` and navigate while the brief save is still in flight. A failed or interrupted IndexedDB save is therefore recorded as a completed dossier, undermining the analytics validation. These handlers should be async, await persistence, then capture completion/navigate.

```ts
      void saveProjectBriefForFolio(store.folioId, next);
      void captureProductEvent("dossier_completed", { mode: "refine" });
      void nav("/editor/");
```

6. `logic_error` — severity 2, confidence 0.90  
Location: `src/routes/editor/index.tsx`  
“Milestone reached” state is only session-local. `editedFolios` starts empty on every page load and is explicitly cleared whenever a folio is loaded, so every reopen/switch followed by an edit emits another `first_edit`. Word thresholds also re-emit whenever text falls below and crosses a threshold again. Since no folio identifier is sent, downstream analytics cannot reliably deduplicate these events per draft.

```ts
    const loadFolioHandler = (e: Event) => {
      if (!store.activeFolioId) return;
      const html = (e as CustomEvent).detail as string;
      lastWordCounts.set(store.activeFolioId, countDraftWords(html));
      editedFolios.delete(store.activeFolioId);
    };
```

7. `resource_leakage` — severity 2, confidence 0.91  
Location: `packages/twyne-tools/src/cli.ts`  
The hidden-token prompt puts stdin into raw mode but restores it only for Ctrl-C or newline. It has no `end`, `error`, or signal cleanup; Ctrl-D is ignored in raw mode. EOF/error can therefore leave the promise pending and the terminal in raw mode.

```ts
    const cleanup = () => {
      input.off("data", onData);
      input.setRawMode(wasRaw);
      input.pause();
      io.stdout.write("\n");
    };
    const onData = (chunk: Buffer | string) => {
      for (const character of String(chunk)) {
        if (character === "\u0003") {
          cleanup();
          reject(new Error("Login cancelled"));
          return;
        }
        if (character === "\r" || character === "\n") {
          cleanup();
          resolve(value.trim());
          return;
        }
        if (character === "\u007f" || character === "\b") {
          value = value.slice(0, -1);
        } else if (character >= " ") {
          value += character;
        }
      }
    };
    input.setRawMode(true);
    input.resume();
    input.on("data", onData);
```

No finding: `correctness_syntax_issues`. Full TypeScript checking with incremental output disabled and `tools:check` both passed. Focused tests passed except two config tests blocked solely by the read-only `/tmp` sandbox.

